column2:
Telemachus, you need no longer be bashful, not even a little;
15	for this very reason you sailed over the sea, that you might learn
16	of your father, where the earth covered him and what fate he met.
17	But come now, go straight to Nestor, tamer of horses;
18	let us see what counsel he keeps hidden in his breast.
19	And beseech him yourself, that he may speak unerringly;
20	and a lie he will not tell, for he is very wise.

Mentor, how shall I go? How shall I greet him?
23	I have no experience yet of close-packed speeches;
24	and there is shame for a young man to question an older one.

Old man, I do not think this word will yet be fulfilled;
227	for you have said too great a thing; awe holds me. It could not happen
228	for me, even in my hope, not even if the gods so wished.
